From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:45:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] A battle's start's last step all black, not every other slice white (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The slices of a battle's start (ScreenSlice) end with them moved 255
pixels. Window 1, which hides the part of a slice moved right, then has
its right edge at 256, which the register's 8 bits keep as 0: the window
hid nothing, so for that step every other slice showed what's behind the
3D, white on the field, before the screen went black. On the DS that
step lasts a 30th of a second and its screen hardly shows it; on the 3DS
it was plain to see. The edge is now at most 255, which on the 3DS
reaches the screen's edge (windowsToEdge): those slices black too.

---
diff --git a/src/overlay005/encounter_effect.c b/src/overlay005/encounter_effect.c
index b0f995eb..56de5baa 100644
--- a/src/overlay005/encounter_effect.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/encounter_effect.c
@@ -494,6 +494,28 @@ static void ScreenSliceSystem_VBlankCallback(SysTask *task, void *param)
 
         s32 currentX = screenSliceEfx->interpolationTask.currentValue >> FX32_SHIFT;
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+        /* (window 1's right edge, the part of a slice moved right it
+         * hides: at the last step, slices moved 255, it's 256, which the
+         * register's 8 bits keep as 0, and window 1 then hid nothing: for
+         * that step every other slice showed what's behind the 3D, white
+         * on the field. At most 255, which on the 3DS reaches the screen's
+         * edge (windowsToEdge): those slices black too, as the effect means
+         * them to go) */
+        {
+            s32 win1Right = currentX >= 0 ? 1 + currentX : 1 - currentX;
+
+            if (win1Right > 255) {
+                win1Right = 255;
+            }
+            if (currentX >= 0) {
+                G2_SetWnd0Position(0, 0, 255 - currentX, 192);
+            } else {
+                G2_SetWnd0Position(0, 0, 255 + currentX, 192);
+            }
+            G2_SetWnd1Position(0, 0, win1Right, 192);
+        }
+#else
         if (currentX >= 0) {
             G2_SetWnd0Position(0, 0, 255 - currentX, 192);
             G2_SetWnd1Position(0, 0, 1 + currentX, 192);
@@ -501,6 +523,7 @@ static void ScreenSliceSystem_VBlankCallback(SysTask *task, void *param)
             G2_SetWnd0Position(0, 0, 255 + currentX, 192);
             G2_SetWnd1Position(0, 0, 1 - currentX, 192);
         }
+#endif
         break;
     case SCREENSLICE_STATE_FINISH:
         ScreenSliceEffect_Finish(param);
